            <div xml:id="d864">

                <pb facs="1063" n="1055" sameAs="frus:frus1938v02/pg1055"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.6731/343a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Chargé in Turkey</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Kelley</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-03-07T12:00:00-05:00">March 7, 1938—noon</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>26. Henry J. Wadleigh of the Division of Trade Agreements, Department of State,
                    and Mr. Norman R. Burns of the United States Tariff Commission have been
                    designated members of the delegation to negotiate a trade agreement with Turkey
                    at Ankara. They will sail from New York on the S. S. <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Washington</hi> on March 9. Mr. Gillespie, who will be the Department of
                    Commerce’s member on the delegation, will sail on the S. S. <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Bremen</hi> on March 12. All will arrive in Ankara
                    before March 28. Negotiations should commence if possible on that day, and you
                    are requested to make all necessary arrangements to this end, including hotel
                    reservations. Kelley is hereby designated chief of the delegation and
                        Gillespie<anchor n="5" xml:id="d864-f1"/> his alternate.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d864-f1" n="5" xml:id="d864-f1-content">
                <p>Julian E. Gillespie, Commercial Attaché in Turkey.</p>
            </note>
